## Test Case Specification
{step:design-tests}

Implement the designed unit and integration tests. Use the repository's existing test conventions and reusable fixtures. Write table-driven tests where cases share logic, use t.Helper() for helpers, and t.Cleanup() for teardown. Ensure every failure message includes function name, inputs, got, and want. Run the new tests to confirm they compile and pass. Do not modify production code unless a test exposes a real defect; if so, report it explicitly.

